-- title:
--   Reduction of Igusa-scheme points matches the fibre model's specialisation of places
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\ell$ is a prime, $p$ a nonzero natural number with $\ell \nmid p$ (hypothesis `hℓp`), and $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ denotes the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. The Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme p ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is the pushout of the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebras `chartAlgFin p ℓ` and `chartAlgInf p ℓ`, the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras of the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $j(q^{d})$ for $d \mid p$) formed of the elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$, respectively over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$; `igusaTo p ℓ` is its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, and `ιFin p ℓ`, `ιInf p ℓ` are the two chart morphisms from the spectra of the chart algebras into it. A `CurveModel K L` consists of an integral scheme $C$ proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} K$, an isomorphism of $L$ with the function field of $C$ over $K$, and a bijection of the closed points of $C$ with the set of places of $L/K$ (a place being a valuation subring of $L$ containing $K$, distinct from $L$, whose ring is a principal ideal ring), compatibly with the stalks; when $K$ is algebraically closed, `pointEquivPlace` is the induced bijection between the sections of the structure morphism and the places.
--
--   Generic data. `Mη` is a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $F$; `eη` is a morphism from `Mη.C` to the pullback of `igusaTo p ℓ` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, assumed to be an isomorphism, and `heη` requires that `eη` followed by the second pullback projection be `Mη.toBase`.
--
--   Generic centre pins `hgenFin`, `hgenInf`. For every section $x$ of `Mη.toBase` and every ring homomorphism $\gamma$ from `chartAlgFin p ℓ` (respectively `chartAlgInf p ℓ`) to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $x$ followed by `eη` followed by the first pullback projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\gamma)$ followed by `ιFin p ℓ` (respectively `ιInf p ℓ`), it is required that for every $b$ in that chart algebra the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` obtained from $b \in F$ by the coefficient embedding lies in the valuation subring of the place `Mη.pointEquivPlace x`, and that this element minus the constant $\gamma(b)$ lies in the nonunits of that valuation subring.
--
--   Special-fibre data over all places above $\ell$. A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies over $\ell$, in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, when $\ell$ is a nonunit of $A$. For each such $A$ there are given: a ring homomorphism $\rho_A \colon \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to A$ with `hρ` asserting that composing it with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ gives the structure map of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$; a curve model $M_{s,A}$ over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField ↥A) p` (the $\kappa_A$-subfield of $\kappa_A((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid p$, in characteristic $\ell$); a morphism `es A hA` from $M_{s,A}.C$ to the pullback of `igusaTo p ℓ` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_A$ followed by the residue map, assumed an isomorphism (`hes_iso`) and satisfying `hes`, namely that composing it with the second pullback projection gives $M_{s,A}.\mathrm{toBase}$.
--
--   A particular $A$ with $\ell$ a nonunit is then fixed, with $\kappa_A$ of characteristic $\ell$ and algebraically closed. Further data: `dataAll`, assigning to each divisor $d$ of $p$ a `ModularPolynomialData d`, that is a monic polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree the Dedekind $\psi(d)$ in $Y$ that kills $j(q^{d})$ over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$; `hsep`, requiring that the reduction of $\Phi$ for $d = p$ modulo $\ell$, viewed over $\kappa_A(X)$, be separable; `hCF`, the equality `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField ↥A) p = modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField ↥A) p` of the subfield generated by $j$ and $j(q^{p})$ with the full one; a fibre model `fm : FibreModel p A ℓ κ_A (residue A)`, consisting of two subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_\infty$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` containing the constants from $A$ and $j$, $j(q^{p})$, respectively $j^{-1}$, with integrality conditions over the corresponding affine base rings, together with reduction homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}} \colon B_{\mathrm{fin}} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` and $\pi_\infty \colon B_\infty \to$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` compatible with the residue map on constants and sending $j$, $j(q^{p})$, $j^{-1}$ to their characteristic-$\ell$ expansions; and `cc : fm.CuspChart`, asserting that $j(q^{p}) \cdot (j^{-1})^{p}$ lies in $B_\infty$ and that $\pi_\infty$ sends it to the corresponding product in characteristic $\ell$.
--
--   Chart containments `hfin`, `hinf`: the coefficient-embedded image of every element of `chartAlgFin p ℓ` lies in `fm.BFin`, and that of every element of `chartAlgInf p ℓ` lies in `fm.BInf`.
--
--   Special centre pins `hspFin`, `hspInf`. For every section $y$ of $M_{s,A}.\mathrm{toBase}$ and every ring homomorphism $\beta$ from `chartAlgFin p ℓ` (respectively `chartAlgInf p ℓ`) to $\kappa_A$ such that $y$ followed by `es A hA` followed by the first pullback projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\beta)$ followed by `ιFin p ℓ` (respectively `ιInf p ℓ`), it is required that for every $b$ in that chart algebra the element $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (respectively $\pi_\infty$) of the coefficient-embedded $b$, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A p` through the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldC_le_full`, lies in the valuation subring of the place $M_{s,A}.$`pointEquivPlace` $y$, and that this element minus the constant $\beta(b)$ lies in the nonunits of that valuation subring.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $xA$, that is every morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `IgusaScheme p ℓ` whose composite with `igusaTo p ℓ` is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_A$, every section $x$ of `Mη.toBase` and every section $y$ of $M_{s,A}.\mathrm{toBase}$ such that $x$ followed by `eη` followed by the first pullback projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $xA$, and such that $y$ followed by `es A hA` followed by the first pullback projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map of $A$ followed by $xA$, the place attached to $y$ satisfies
--   $$M_{s,A}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\, y = \mathrm{congrRingEquiv}\bigl(\mathrm{IntermediateField.equivOfEq}\ \mathrm{hCF}\bigr)\bigl(\mathrm{fm}.\mathrm{spPlace}(\mathrm{dataAll}, \mathrm{hsep})(\mathrm{Mη}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\, x)\bigr),$$
--   where `fm.spPlace`, formed with the surjectivity of the residue map, `dataAll` and `hsep`, carries places of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` over $\kappa_A$, and `congrRingEquiv` transports a place along the isomorphism of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A p` with `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A p` given by the equality `hCF` (which fixes $\kappa_A$), by taking the preimage of the valuation subring under the inverse isomorphism.
--
--   The statement expresses that, in the centre-pinned setting, reduction of points from the generic to the special fibre of the Igusa scheme is computed by the specialisation map on places attached to a fibre model with cusp chart: a section of the generic model and a section of the special model which come from one and the same $A$-point of the Igusa scheme have places related by `fm.spPlace`. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport model package, where reduction data are matched with crossing points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_pointReduction_eq_congr_spPlace_of_cuspChart_centrePin.lean

